---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="DIY Move vs Professional Movers — Relocation Cost"
  description="Compare a DIY move, a rental truck with hired labor and full-service movers on cost, effort, risk and flexibility, plus the questions to ask before you choose."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-600">Guide</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">DIY vs professional movers</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">The cheaper headline price is not the whole comparison. Time, equipment, labor, travel and risk all matter. This guide lays out the trade-offs so you can choose with the full picture.</p>

    <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] text-left text-sm leading-6">
        <thead class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
          <tr><th class="p-4 font-semibold">Factor</th><th class="p-4 font-semibold">DIY</th><th class="p-4 font-semibold">Professional movers</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-slate-600">
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><th class="p-4 align-top font-semibold text-slate-900">Cash cost</th><td class="p-4 align-top">Usually lower, but you pay for the truck, fuel and equipment.</td><td class="p-4 align-top">Higher, because labor and service are included.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><th class="p-4 align-top font-semibold text-slate-900">Your time and effort</th><td class="p-4 align-top">You plan, pack, load, drive and unload.</td><td class="p-4 align-top">Much less physical work and driving for you.</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><th class="p-4 align-top font-semibold text-slate-900">Risk</th><td class="p-4 align-top">Damage, delays and mistakes are yours to manage.</td><td class="p-4 align-top">Shared with the company. Ask exactly what coverage is included.</td></tr>
          <tr><th class="p-4 align-top font-semibold text-slate-900">Flexibility</th><td class="p-4 align-top">More control over timing and what goes on the truck.</td><td class="p-4 align-top">Depends on the company's schedule and its terms.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Costs people forget about a DIY move</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li>Fuel and tolls for a heavy truck, which usually uses more fuel than a car.</li>
      <li>Lodging and meals on the road if the trip takes more than a day.</li>
      <li>Equipment such as dollies, straps and blankets, and packing supplies.</li>
      <li>Coverage for your belongings and the truck, if you choose to buy it.</li>
      <li>Time off work for packing, loading, driving and unloading.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The middle option: truck plus hired labor</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">You can rent the truck and drive it yourself, but pay helpers to load and unload. This keeps control of the route and timing while removing the heaviest work. In our calculator it appears as “Rental truck + labor”.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Who each option tends to suit</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li><strong>DIY</strong> fits smaller moves, flexible schedules and people who are comfortable driving a large truck and lifting.</li>
      <li><strong>Full-service movers</strong> fit large homes, tight schedules, long distances and moves where you cannot spare the time or physical effort.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Questions to ask before you decide</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li>Is the quote in writing, and is it based on my actual addresses, dates and inventory?</li>
      <li>What exactly is included: packing, loading, fuel, tolls, equipment and coverage?</li>
      <li>What can change the price after the quote, and how is that handled?</li>
      <li>What happens if something is damaged or the delivery is late?</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-8 leading-7 text-slate-700">To model the options side by side, use the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator">calculator</a>, or open a route guide such as <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/moving-cost/ca-to-tx">California to Texas</a> to see all three move types for the same home size. The <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/methodology">methodology page</a> explains how the figures are produced and where they stop being reliable.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
